  "body": "As noted over in https://github.com/garykac/procspec/issues/13 there are a few places in HTML that \"return but continue running these steps in parallel\", as opposed to running (sub)steps in parallel and returning as the last step in the algorithm. @annevk noted this was \"weird\".\r\n\r\nA couple examples:\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#downloading-hyperlinks\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#dom-createimagebitmap\r\n\r\nCtrl+F on the single page version shows 11 hits for \"but continue\"\r\n",
